{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>This day HaShem your Elohim commands you.</b> In the fortieth year he stood and said 'this day' — but is it not forty years since they received the Torah? But our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: let them be beloved upon you as if this day you received them from Sinai." "<b>And in the periciah of</b> Shema (Deuteronomy 6:6), in the verse ״אשר אנכי מצוך היום״, they interpreted: let them be new in your eyes as if this day you received them from Sinai. Whether in the language of 'beloved' or in the language of 'new,' they needed to interpret thus because the generations pass and the heart of man follows his eyes after the visible thing — for when it stands before his eyes he remembers it, and when it is hidden from his eyes he forgets it, and the signs and wonders do not endure forever. Therefore they warned that faith should be fixed in the heart, standing forever at the time of concealment just as it was at the time of revelation, and that the words of Torah should be beloved to us so that we not transgress them, and that they should also be new in the matter of remembering the signs and wonders, so that we not forget them from our heart when they disappear from our eyes — rather, the standing at Mount Sinai with its wonders should be in its newness always upon us." "<b>And it is possible</b> to say that this verse began with 'this day' and concluded with 'ובכל נפשך' ('and with all your soul'), to teach that a person is obligated to surrender his soul for the commandments in all times, every one of them, like the day of the giving of the Torah. For just as he would have surrendered his soul for HaShem on that very day of the giving of the Torah, when he saw the signs and wonders and the consuming fire on the top of the mountain, so too it is fitting for him to surrender his soul for Him in all times, every one of them — and this is what it said: 'this day,' and concluded with 'your soul,' to explain that you shall surrender your soul for Him in all times, every one of them, like this day."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:51:23.088917822Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}